    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9260" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνοος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνους</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ουν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without
				understanding, silly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κραδίη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					21.441
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					44a
				</span></i>
			, etc.; of persons, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				99
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνους τε καὶ γέρων
			ἅμα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				281
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλοῦτος ἄ.</span> wealth
				<i>without wit,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				9.43
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Parmen.
			</span></i>): 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνούστερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					987
				</span></i>
			: 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνούστατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pherecr.
					19D.
				</span></i>
			
			Adv., 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνουστέρως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					589.1
				</span></i>
			.</div>
